# API Integration

**Source of truth:** `docs/user-journey-api.md`

## Request headers

| Route group | Headers |
|-------------|---------|
| Public auth | none |
| Tenant (`/clients`, `/projects`, …) | `Authorization` + `X-Freelancer-Id` |
| Portal (`/portal/*`) | `Authorization` + `X-Client-Id` |
| Admin (`/admin/*`) | `Authorization` only |
| Subscription | `Authorization` + `X-Freelancer-Id` |

Use `apiRequest()` from `lib/api.ts` — never raw `fetch` in features.

## Cursor pagination

All list endpoints return:

```typescript
type PaginatedResponse<T> = {
  data: T[]
  links: { first: string; prev: string | null; next: string | null }
  meta: { per_page: number; next_cursor: string | null; prev_cursor: string | null }
}
```

Pass `cursor` and `per_page` (default 25, max 100) as query params. Use shared `CursorPagination` component.

## Error handling

| HTTP | code | UI action |
|------|------|-----------|
| 401 | `unauthenticated` | clear token, redirect `/login` |
| 403 | `workspace_read_only` | show ReadOnlyBanner, disable write buttons |
| 403 | `forbidden` | toast + hide action |
| 422 | `validation_failed` | map `errors` to form fields |
| 422 | `plan_limit_exceeded` | upgrade prompt |

Parse `ApiError.body` — never show raw stack traces.

## Types

Mirror API resource names in feature `types.ts`. Shared pagination/auth types live in `src/types/api.ts`.
